# The shop bench's budgets, fixed before the first measurement (run-log 235). test/bench/budget reads this file.
# A "check" line fails the run when the value is over; a "report" line is printed against its budget only, since wall
# time depends on the machine (these were set for an Apple M2 laptop, z3 on PATH, --jobs 4, an empty cache).
#
# Questions: the scripts the solver ran from an empty cache. 120 s of prove at --jobs 4 is 480 solver-seconds; the
# 3-service bench's questions average 0.12 s of wall time each at --jobs 4, so about 1500 questions fit.
check prove.questions 1500
check generate.questions 1500
# Every question decides at the default resource limit.
check prove.undecided 0
check generate.undecided 0
# The largest script and all of prove's scripts together, in bytes. z3 read a 12 MB response script in about 0.9 s
# (run-log 224), so 16 MiB keeps one script's reading near a second, and 512 MiB keeps prove's reading near 10 s at
# --jobs 4.
check script.max_bytes 16777216
check prove.script_bytes 536870912
# Wall time in seconds.
report check.seconds 5
report prove.cold.seconds 120
report prove.cached.seconds 10
report generate.seconds 300
